{
  "name": "Maternal/child health project Umeed-e-Nau launched in 14 districts of Pakistan",
  "parent_id": 203313630673674,
  "group_id": "9c4636e1-a119-4844-835c-9917e70d5151",
  "alternates": [],
  "created_at": "2026-07-30T14:52:55.953Z",
  "deleted_at": null,
  "sort_by_date": null,
  "tag_list": [],
  "updated_at": "2026-08-12T15:02:58.481Z",
  "published_at": "2026-08-12T15:02:58.465Z",
  "id": 203708727146229,
  "uuid": "36bacf12-bf97-4847-8610-33bc23fe9c36",
  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "e5c5bdea-a83d-68d4-ff32-78f7ac3df21e",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "03c11636-7312-b763-fb3c-7cd54eaf401a",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Funded by a US$25 million grant from the Bill & Melinda Gates Foundation, Umeed-e-Nau (new hope) is a five-year project that will see AKU work with public sector programmes and primary care providers such as Lady Health Workers and Community Health Midwives to deliver proven interventions and improve the quality of care at health facilities in 14 mainly rural districts in Balochistan, Southern Punjab and Sindh, as well as urban slums in Karachi.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The districts include Badin, Dadu, Hyderabad/Matiari, Karachi, Jafferabad, Jamshoro, Lasbela, Mirpur Khas, Muzaffargarh, Nasirabad, Qambar Shahdadkot, Rahim Yar Khan, Sanghar and Thatta. The project also includes a groundbreaking effort to provide health education through schools for adolescent girls in Pakistan.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "\"Federal and provincial governments, public and private institutions, civil society and every one of us have to team up to meet the United Nation's 17 Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) by 2030,\" said Professor Zulfiqar Bhutta, Founding Director of the Aga Khan University's Centre of Excellence in Women and Child Health. \"Projects like Umeed-e-Nau can help Pakistan achieve Goal 3 for health, which also requires additional investments in improving nutrition, keeping children in schools and addressing environmental health and gender equity.\" ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Speaking by video link, Dr Christopher Elias, President of the Global Development Programme at the Bill and Melinda Gates Foundation spoke about the range of initiatives set to be introduced through the grant.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Dr Elias said: \"Proven interventions like clean birthing kits, training on neonatal resuscitation and oral rehydration for diarrhea will be delivered. New approaches to service delivery will also be tested such as social support groups for Kangaroo mothercare, strategies to improve immunisation demand and better access to pulse oximetry to improve pneumonia diagnosis and increase referrals by lady health workers.\"",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The project will operate through a new research centre, the Centre of Excellence, Women and Child Health, which will be established through a generous gift of Rs 2 billion from the Hashoo Foundation.",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Muhammad Ayub Shaikh, Secretary, Ministry of National Health Sciences, Regulations and Coordination, Government of Pakistan, expressed their commitment to join hands with AKU and accelerate progress.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "\"Umeed-e-Nau will test a variety of approaches in an effort to develop insights and evidence that can influence policy across the country and beyond its borders,\" Professor Bhutta added. \"We believe that the project will reduce stillbirths and newborn deaths by 20 per cent, as well as deaths from pneumonia and diarrhoea by 30 per cent through these strategies.\"",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "AKU President Firoz Rasul thanked the Bill & Melinda Gates Foundation for its partnership and support to improve maternal and child health in Pakistan.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "\"As part of its activities to support the Sustainable Development Goals, AKU has pledged to invest more than US$85 million over the next decade in support of the Global Strategy for Women's, Children's and Adolescents' Health, which is designed to help achieve Goal 3 of SDGs,\" President Rasul said.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The ceremony was also attended by AKU donors, members of the Hashoo Foundation, and Dr Muhammad Usman Chachar, Secretary of Health, Government of Sindh.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
